lines=['# Motion: small scene calibration experiment','','## Decision','','**Reject this calibration recipe and stop before candidate validation or test.** All6seed/horizon combinations worsen held-out training-pair common-residual error. Both predeclared seed-mean predictability checks fail. This is a failed feasibility screen, not a new score for the original51prediction checks.','','![Cross-validation result](../results/motion_scene_calibration/crossfit_result.png)','','The bars show the percent increase in the COMMON-residual fitting target error, not total forecasting error or task accuracy. Lower is better; every bar is above zero. Six combinations reuse the same training pairs and are not six independent datasets.','','## What was trained','','The user approved only small calibration heads while keeping all original predictors, encoder, basis, decoder, data and acceptance thresholds fixed. Inputs are128frozen projected-current features and6known-action summaries. The head predicts a correction restricted to the126position-null directions inside the existing128output basis. For identical paired current/action context, its correction is identical, preserving the original prediction contrast and decoded position algebraically. It is not a retention policy.','','Training labels are paired COMMON residuals: average the two training siblings of target feature minus frozen baseline forecast. Targets are allowed training labels; future features, sibling IDs and simulator states are not deployment inputs. All512original training pairs and3base seeds are retained.','','The fixed protocol uses two pair-disjoint folds (seed0):256pairs fit and256held out, swapped once. Each of the512pairs is held out exactly once. One ridge coefficient,0.01times the average normalized training Gram diagonal, and train-fold-only scaling are used. No gradient-based optimization, epoch search, parameter grid or base-model update. The12fold solutions are temporary feasibility fits; because the screen fails, the6final full-training heads are not fitted or deployed. Original completed120epoch models are unchanged.','','The original base models were previously trained on all512training pairs. These folds hold pairs out only from CALIBRATION fitting, not from base-model training. The screen assesses the proposed head conditional on that fixed base; it is not independent whole-pipeline confirmation.','','## Complete six-combination results','','| Base seed | Horizon | Before common-residual MSE | After held-out MSE | Increase |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x,v in zip(c['cells'],vals):lines.append(f"|{x['seed']}|{x['horizon']}|{x['before']:.8f}|{x['after']:.8f}|{v:.2f}%|")
lines+=['','Both seed-mean absolute gains are negative: h3 '+f"{c['mean_absolute_gain']['3']:.8f}"+' and h6 '+f"{c['mean_absolute_gain']['6']:.8f}"+'. These values trigger the prospectively declared stop. No new original acceptance threshold is introduced.','','## Execution and independent verification','','Read-only CPU preflight packed1,024training episodes and1,152existing validation cache rows, checked exact paired-context identity and source hashes, and performed no model forward or fitting. Existing validation arrays were prepacked for provenance and a possible later evaluation; no validation target entered fitting, and no calibrated candidate validation/test evaluation occurred.','','GPU8496ran on an actualA100-SXM4-40GB with4scientific threads. It produced frozen training forecasts and solved the train-fold ridge systems on CUDA. Original model-state digests match before/after. GPUjob completed with exit0:0; that execution success is distinct from the scientific rejection.','','A separate CPU auditing program evaluated the fixed CUDA coefficients and their ridge normal equations, without refitting any scientific model. It independently rebuilt every held-out crossfit error. Maximum normalized equation residual '+f"{a['normal_equation_max_relative_error']:.3g}"+'; position-null leakage '+f"{a['position_null_max']:.3g}"+'. Five synthetic software fixtures are software evidence only. All27final compact native-before/local/native-after hashes match. Arrays and temporary weights remainHPC.','',f"A separate frozen CPU replay of36training forecast vectors (6distinct training episodes,3base seeds,2horizons) checked the actual CUDA residual construction. Maximum common-residual MSE difference {vr['scalar_max_difference']:.3g}, within unchanged2e-6precision tolerance; descriptive vector maximum difference {vr['vector_max_difference_descriptive']:.3g}. Five additional verification files have matching transfer hashes. No additional scientific fitting or GPU.",'','The additional matched recent-only calibration diagnostic was predeclared but not run: it requires final heads, which were not fitted after rejection. No inference about its outcome is made.','','## Budget','','Native Slurm settlement: **'+str(b['new_GPU_seconds'])+'newGPU seconds**, within the600second stage hardcap. Cumulative **'+str(b['settled_seconds'])+'/'+str(b['total_cap_seconds'])+'seconds**, leaving **'+str(b['remaining_seconds'])+'seconds (4h27m15s)**. Failed feasibility work is included. No furtherGPU was submitted after the stop.','','## What this establishes','','This specified linear calibration, with current/action inputs and its fixed regularization, does not generalize even across training-pair folds. A numerical solver failure is not indicated by the independent normal-equation audit. The result does not prove that every calibration architecture or input choice must fail, and it does not isolate missing information from regularization/model-class limitations. Do not tune another coefficient or add an input using these outcomes under this completed protocol.','','The prior best explored Motion composite remains a separate48/51original prediction,29/32fixed-reference,8/8critical long-gap and69/72deletion result. No improved model has been adopted. Gate was not changed or reevaluated here. **OverallPhase1_GO remains unestablished; no fresh9137confirmation or retention-policy training was started.** No GitHub update. The scope is this controlled synthetic Motion task with frozen5,120-dimensional I-JEPA features; no V-JEPA or real-video validation is established.']
